      <p><strong>Spa management software runs a spa or wellness centre from one system: online booking, therapist and room scheduling, payments, discounts and reports. A good one books the therapist, the room and the time together, so none is double-booked. Zennly is spa management software built for multi-branch spas.</strong></p>

      <h2>What makes a spa different</h2>
      <p>A treatment needs a person and a room for a set length of time. If either is tracked on paper or in a chat, clashes happen. Spa software books the therapist, room and time as one booking, so a guest is never confirmed for a slot that cannot happen.</p>

      <h2>Features worth looking for</h2>
      <p>These are the features that matter most as a spa gets busier:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Online booking that shows real therapist and room availability</li>
        <li>Therapist and room scheduling in one booking, with clashes refused</li>
        <li>Different durations for different treatments</li>
        <li>Payments recorded by method (cash, card, online), including part-payments</li>
        <li>Discount requests that a manager approves, with an audit trail</li>
        <li>A daily close that matches recorded payments to money received</li>
        <li>Reports for revenue, staff performance and discounts across every location</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Spas with more than one location</h2>
      <p>A second spa location adds new problems: therapists who work at both, price differences and an owner who cannot see every site at once. Look for software that schedules staff transfers in advance and gives one dashboard for all locations. See <a href="/blog/multi-location-booking-software/">multi-location booking software</a> and our guide to <a href="/blog/how-to-manage-a-spa-in-nepal/">managing a spa</a>.</p>

      <h2>Common mistakes when choosing spa software</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Booking a time slot without checking the therapist and the room together</li>
        <li>Setting every treatment to the same length, so rooms are blocked too long or too short</li>
        <li>Letting discounts go unrecorded because the system has no approval step</li>
        <li>Having no daily close, so the end of the day is spent hunting for missing payments</li>
        <li>Forgetting that a second location needs staff who can work at both</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Fixing these early keeps the spa calm on busy days and keeps the owner's numbers trustworthy.</p>

      <h2>Questions to ask before you buy</h2>
      <p>Ask about setup fees, how pricing changes with more therapists, rooms or locations, support and training, data export, and how payments, taxes and memberships or vouchers are handled in your country. Ask for a demo with your own treatment menu.</p>

      <h2>Spa, wellness center or wellness centre?</h2>
      <p>These describe the same kind of business. 'Center' is the US spelling and 'centre' is used in the UK, Canada, Australia, the UAE and Nepal. The software is the same.</p>

      <h2>Where Zennly fits</h2>
      <p>Zennly is built for multi-branch spas, with therapist and room booking, discount approval, payment tracking and a daily close. Nuad Thai Spa Kathmandu runs four branches on it. If you run a single treatment room, a simpler calendar may be enough. See <a href="/solutions/spa/">how Zennly works for spas</a> and the <a href="/case-study/">Nuad Thai case study</a>.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What is spa management software?</h3>
      <p>It is software that runs a spa's online booking, therapist and room scheduling, payments, discounts and reports in one system.</p>
      <h3>What features does spa software need?</h3>
      <p>Therapist and room booking in one, clash prevention, treatment durations, payments by method, discount approval and reports. Multi-location spas also need staff transfers and one dashboard.</p>
      <h3>Do I need spa management software for one location?</h3>
      <p>A single room can run on a simple calendar. Software pays off when you have several therapists and rooms, or plan a second location.</p>

